":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:4eb1726a022c30330534d260a55926a385c3f4ec6b2f05103bb8861a4464296a","file":"preprints/The-Gaussian-free-field-limit-of-integer-Lipschitz-heights-with-two-arc-boundary-data-October-6-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":47,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5cd0002c4b0e52615903648a1913c147a59d4594f2e5f9393806b933e70667d7","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Gaussian-free-field-limit-of-integer-Lipschitz-heights-with-two-arc-boundary-data-October-6-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:4eb1726a022c30330534d260a55926a385c3f4ec6b2f05103bb8861a4464296a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Gaussian-free-field-limit-of-integer-Lipschitz-heights-with-two-arc-boundary-data-October-6-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L47"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $D$ be a bounded smooth simply connected planar domain with two\ndistinct marked boundary points.  Let $D_\\delta$ be simply connected\ntriangular-lattice polygonal approximations with uniformly converging\nmarked boundary parametrizations and edge-midpoint marks, and let\n$h_\\delta$ have the uniform odd-height law \\eqref{eq:odd-model}.\nThere is a constant $\\sigma>0$, depending only on the unit triangular-lattice\nmodel, such that\n\\[\n h_\\delta\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ \\bar g+\\sigma\\Phi_D\n \\qquad\\text{in }\\mathcal D'(D).\n\\]\nFor every $f\\in C_c^\\infty(D)$, $\\EE h_\\delta(f)\\to\\int_D\\bar g f$.\nConsequently\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main-centered}\n \\frac{h_\\delta-\\EE h_\\delta}{\\sigma}\n \\ \\Longrightarrow\\ \\Phi_D\n \\qquad\\text{in }\\mathcal D'(D).\n\\end{equation}\nAll finite vectors of test-function integrals converge jointly to the\ncorresponding Gaussian vectors, and all their mixed moments converge.\nThe constant is specified by the absolutely convergent finite-volume series\nin \\cref{prop:normalization-series}; in the spectral convention below,\n$\\sigma=4\\pi\\sqrt{c_*}$."}
